.TH MOVE_PAGES 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
move_pages \- Linux x86-64 syscall 279
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B long move_pages(pid_t process, unsigned long count, void** pages, const int* nodes, int* status, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries or migrates pages across NUMA nodes; privileges and kernel support vary.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR move_pages (2)
